# UI Quality First

Read `docs/DESIGN_CONSTITUTION.md` before any user-facing UI work.

## Requirements

- Less but better: whitespace, one primary CTA, short copy
- Visual hierarchy: do now → AI understands → review → next action
- Card-first; no border spam
- Review Board vocabulary only (no "결과", GO/HOLD, fake scores)
- Editable understanding rows with save + toast feedback
- UI Self Review must pass before ship; include Before/After screenshots in release report

## Bad Examples

- Split panels with redundant status cards
- Decorative icons and emoji progress bars
- Long disclaimer paragraphs
- Multiple equal-weight CTAs
